cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its findings, please cite the paper below."
title: "LLOGIC: Measuring Logical Inconsistency of Large Language Models over OWL Ontologies"
abstract: >-
  A three-phase empirical framework that compiles LLM-generated first-order-logic
  statements into a Z3 SMT solver to measure whether large language models stay
  logically consistent when defining and relating concepts in formal OWL/SKOS
  ontologies. Central finding: LLM inconsistency is relational, not definitional.
